  "question": {
    "text": "A solid sphere is in pure rolling motion on an inclined surface having inclination $\\theta$.\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/SqpFTGNOh5r0Id1yrfTHMgHqm61n25jCGlaCyaWC2gQ.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "4NISm",
      "text": "\nfrictional force acting on sphere is $f=\\mu m g \\cos \\theta$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "KHsEk",
      "text": "\n$f$ is disspative force\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "vEOpc",
      "text": "\nfriction will increase its angular velocity and decreases its linear velocity\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "9YZFx",
      "text": "\nIf $\\theta$ decreases, friction will decrease",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "In case of pure rolling,\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& f=\\frac{m g \\sin \\theta}{1+\\frac{m R^2}{I}} \\\\\n\\therefore & f \\propto \\sin \\theta\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n(upwards)\nTherefore, as $\\theta$ decreases force of friction will also decrease.",
    "image": null
  },
